{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\hist\\074.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Unit04", "conf": 0.852, "box": [[340, 113], [389, 113], [389, 130], [340, 130]]}, {"text": "Muslims inSouthAsia", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[392, 111], [534, 107], [534, 127], [393, 132]]}, {"text": "The Mongol Invasion", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[65, 152], [307, 152], [307, 178], [65, 178]]}, {"text": "AlauddinKhilji DefencePoliciesAgainstMongol Invasions", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[61, 195], [570, 192], [570, 216], [61, 219]]}, {"text": "During the reign of Alauddin Khiji. Mongols invaded India seven times, but Alauddin", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[57, 233], [840, 217], [840, 251], [57, 266]]}, {"text": "succeeded in defeating them every time. Alauddin Khilji planned to defend the empire by", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[55, 259], [840, 245], [840, 277], [55, 291]]}, {"text": "formulatinga strongand systematicfrontierpolicy.", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[58, 286], [491, 284], [491, 307], [58, 309]]}, {"text": "Old forts were restored, new forts were built and skilled troops under capable", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[112, 316], [838, 305], [838, 336], [113, 346]]}, {"text": "officerswere posted.Theirmilitarypower was also enhanced.", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[114, 344], [644, 338], [644, 364], [114, 370]]}, {"text": "Factoriesweresetuptoproducearmaments.", "conf": 0.943, "box": [[116, 384], [499, 384], [499, 404], [116, 404]]}, {"text": "A permanent army was organized for the defence of the North-West Frontier and a", "conf": 0.871, "box": [[113, 422], [837, 412], [837, 439], [113, 448]]}, {"text": "special governorwas appointed there.", "conf": 0.869, "box": [[114, 448], [439, 445], [440, 469], [114, 472]]}, {"text": "iv.", "conf": 0.737, "box": [[58, 488], [84, 488], [84, 511], [58, 511]]}, {"text": "Separate armies were stationed in the frontier areas of Dipalpur, Samana and", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[112, 484], [788, 477], [788, 507], [112, 514]]}, {"text": "Multan.", "conf": 0.806, "box": [[114, 514], [183, 514], [183, 534], [114, 534]]}, {"text": "Alauddin's frontierpolicyprovedverysuccessful.TheMongols ceased theiraggression", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[59, 536], [811, 530], [811, 557], [59, 563]]}, {"text": "during the later years of Alauddin's reign.", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[59, 562], [408, 561], [408, 585], [59, 587]]}, {"text": "Activity:Mongols invaded India several times.", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[98, 607], [490, 606], [490, 629], [98, 630]]}, {"text": "1.", "conf": 0.662, "box": [[150, 639], [172, 639], [172, 661], [150, 661]]}, {"text": "Prepare a timeline of Mongol invasions.", "conf": 0.874, "box": [[203, 637], [543, 635], [543, 659], [203, 661]]}, {"text": "2.", "conf": 0.665, "box": [[149, 666], [172, 666], [172, 690], [149, 690]]}, {"text": "Enlist areas invade by the Mongols.", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[203, 666], [503, 665], [503, 690], [203, 691]]}, {"text": "Tughluq'sRisetoPower(1320-1413AD)", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[60, 738], [523, 735], [523, 762], [60, 766]]}, {"text": "AfterthedeathofAlauddinKhilji in1316,firstMalikKafur andthenMubarakShahseized", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[57, 777], [829, 772], [829, 794], [57, 799]]}, {"text": "the throne.Both were murdered one after another leaving Khusrau Khan, the favourite", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[57, 802], [827, 797], [827, 820], [57, 825]]}, {"text": "slaveof Mubarak Shah as the Sultan.He could not win the favour of people who invited", "conf": 0.88, "box": [[56, 826], [827, 822], [827, 845], [56, 849]]}, {"text": "Governor of Punjab, Ghazi Khan for help. He revolted against Mubarak Khan and sat on", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[55, 849], [827, 847], [827, 874], [55, 876]]}, {"text": "the thronehimself.Ghazi Khan is known as Ghias-ud-Din Tughluq Shah who laid the basis", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[54, 877], [826, 873], [826, 896], [54, 900]]}, {"text": "ofTughluqDynasty in1320AD.", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[54, 902], [322, 901], [322, 924], [54, 925]]}, {"text": "Tughluq Shah was one of the most trusted", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[55, 938], [411, 935], [412, 959], [55, 962]]}, {"text": "generals of AlauddinKhilji.He proved his", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[54, 964], [410, 961], [411, 985], [54, 988]]}, {"text": "skills by successfully defending against", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[53, 988], [412, 987], [412, 1010], [53, 1011]]}, {"text": "Mongols. He ruled the Sultanate skilfully", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[53, 1013], [411, 1011], [411, 1034], [53, 1037]]}, {"text": "and peace prevailed during his reign.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[52, 1039], [410, 1035], [411, 1059], [52, 1062]]}, {"text": "Ghias-ud-Dinpatronized literarymen like", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[53, 1064], [410, 1062], [410, 1084], [53, 1086]]}, {"text": "Amir Khusrau. He also built a strong fort", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[52, 1088], [411, 1086], [411, 1109], [52, 1111]]}, {"text": "called Tughluqabad near Delhi.", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[52, 1113], [318, 1110], [318, 1133], [52, 1137]]}, {"text": "Tomb of Ghais-ud-din Tughluq Shah", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[511, 1128], [763, 1135], [762, 1158], [510, 1152]]}, {"text": "(69)", "conf": 0.761, "box": [[410, 1184], [446, 1184], [446, 1207], [410, 1207]]}]}